60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Since we know first-come is unfair and moving is a hassle, I'm leaning toward something stable. I'll vote for Fixed Desks by Function!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Fixed Desks by Function minimizes the recurring costs of re-wiring and avoids the budget drain of frequent changes. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I'm concerned about the window access, but Fixed Desks by Function allows us to explicitly decide the allocation rather than leaving it to chance. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Stability is non-negotiable for my ergonomics and noise management. Option C is the only one that ensures I don't spend my life adjusting a chair. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I want us to stay connected, and Fixed Desks by Function lets us group people who need to talk the most! I vote for Option C too!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, does that mean we're all in agreement already? I'm happy if everyone is!","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It appears we have reached a consensus. Option C is the most logical choice given the financial and physical constraints we have identified.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"As long as we are transparent about who gets the window seats and the quieter spots, I am completely on board.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"I'm satisfied. As long as we prioritize the sound meter data when assigning those fixed spots, this is the best outcome for everyone.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'm so glad we all agree! Let's make sure we sit in a way that keeps us all talking and happy!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'll just double-check that we're all definitely voting for C then! I'm still voting for Fixed Desks by Function!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,My vote remains Option C. It is the only choice that aligns with our budget and operational efficiency.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I'm still voting for Option C. It's the most responsible way to handle the daylight and fairness issues.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,I'm still voting for Option C. It's the only way to guarantee the physical comfort and stability I need.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm still voting for Option C! It's the best way to keep us close and avoid all that shuffle chaos!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm super happy we all agree! Final vote for Option C!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,My final vote is Option C.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
